      "text": "The full text of \"The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle\" may be available through various digital libraries and academic databases. Here are some key identifiers and resources that may help you and your students locate the book:\n\n### ISBN\n- **ISBN**: 978-1-4926-6854-6\n\nThis ISBN corresponds to the hardcover edition of the book. It can be useful for searching in academic databases or digital libraries.\n\n### Resources\n1. **Wikipedia Entry**: A summary and information about the book can be found on its [Wikipedia page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seven_Deaths_of_Evelyn_Hardcastle). This page may include links to sources or libraries that hold the text.\n\n2. **Critical Overview**: A detailed analysis of the book is accessible at [Open Books](https://openbooks.net/reviews/seven-deaths-of-evelyn-hardcastle), which could provide insights on where to find critical texts or references.\n\n3. **Publisher Page**: The official publisher description is available on [Sourcebooks](https://openbooks.net/books/seven-deaths-of-evelyn-hardcastle), which lists various formats (hardcover, paperback, ebook, audiobook) and might indicate where they can be obtained.\n\n### Suggestions for Digital Access\n- **Library Services**: Students can check their local university library's digital collection. If it's not available, they should inquire about interlibrary loans.\n- **Academic Databases**: Search engines like JSTOR, ProQuest, or Google Scholar might have access to eBook versions.\n- **E-book Retailers**: Services like Amazon, Google Books, or Kobo could provide digital purchase options.\n\nUsing the above information, your students should have better avenues to source the text digitally for their studies.",
